{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PugdzUopxyagpCzbgCixRL","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Context: the Shelf service\n2\t\n3\tA gRPC server (Go, `google.golang.org/grpc`) over a SQLite file. The contract is `proto/toy/v1/shelf.proto`; the\n4\tbehaviour is `REQUIREMENTS.md` / `spec.py`. You build the server; you do not change the proto, the spec, the harness,\n5\tthe generator or this file.\n6\t\n7\t* **Stubs.** `gen/toy/v1/*.pb.go` is produced by `./generate.sh` (buf) from the proto and is rebuilt by every\n8\t  `./check.sh`. Never write or edit anything under `gen/`. Import it as `toyv1 \"example.com/toybuild/gen/toy/v1\"`.\n9\t* **Entry point.** A `package main` at the repository root (`go build -o bin/toy-server .`).\n10\t* **Environment the checker sets.** `PORT`: listen for gRPC on `127.0.0.1:$PORT` (plaintext). `DB_PATH`: the SQLite file;\n11\t  the table `items(id integer primary key autoincrement, name text not null unique, qty integer not null)` already\n12\t  exists (the harness created it): do not create or migrate tables. Use `database/sql` with the pure-Go driver\n13\t  `modernc.org/sqlite` (driver name `\"sqlite\"`; open `file:<DB_PATH>?_pragma=busy_timeout(10000)` and\n14\t  `SetMaxOpenConns(1)`).\n15\t* **Readiness.** The checker waits for the standard health service (`google.golang.org/grpc/health`, registered on the\n16\t  same server) to answer `SERVING` for the empty service name.\n17\t* **Dependencies.** `go.mod` and `go.sum` already list what the build needs (grpc, protobuf, modernc sqlite, health).\n18\t  There is no network and no `go mod tidy` in the gate: use only packages those modules provide.\n19\t* **Legacy acceptance scenarios.** `visible_spec.py` holds the customer's legacy acceptance scenarios; `spec.py` imports them, so the gate runs them. You do not change them.\n20\t* **Gate.** `./check.sh` (generate, build, then the Lattice check of `spec.py`, layers C and D). Exit 0 = done.\n21\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"025f620c-405e-4060-9816-e76d0ba6c1b0","uuid":"5e1d85d1-9b26-444e-a696-99247174c300","timestamp":"2026-10-31T21:30:45.432Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/fj/tl69n2xd067clrqbx31xtrtr0000gn/T/lo-pilot-tp_vbzcy/K-B/repo/CONTEXT.md","content":"# Context: the Shelf service\n\nA gRPC server (Go, `google.golang.org/grpc`) over a SQLite file. The contract is `proto/toy/v1/shelf.proto`; the\nbehaviour is `REQUIREMENTS.md` / `spec.py`. You build the server; you do not change the proto, the spec, the harness,\nthe generator or this file.\n\n* **Stubs.** `gen/toy/v1/*.pb.go` is produced by `./generate.sh` (buf) from the proto and is rebuilt by every\n  `./check.sh`. Never write or edit anything under `gen/`. Import it as `toyv1 \"example.com/toybuild/gen/toy/v1\"`.\n* **Entry point.** A `package main` at the repository root (`go build -o bin/toy-server .`).\n* **Environment the checker sets.** `PORT`: listen for gRPC on `127.0.0.1:$PORT` (plaintext). `DB_PATH`: the SQLite file;\n  the table `items(id integer primary key autoincrement, name text not null unique, qty integer not null)` already\n  exists (the harness created it): do not create or migrate tables. Use `database/sql` with the pure-Go driver\n  `modernc.org/sqlite` (driver name `\"sqlite\"`; open `file:<DB_PATH>?_pragma=busy_timeout(10000)` and\n  `SetMaxOpenConns(1)`).\n* **Readiness.** The checker waits for the standard health service (`google.golang.org/grpc/health`, registered on the\n  same server) to answer `SERVING` for the empty service name.\n* **Dependencies.** `go.mod` and `go.sum` already list what the build needs (grpc, protobuf, modernc sqlite, health).\n  There is no network and no `go mod tidy` in the gate: use only packages those modules provide.\n* **Legacy acceptance scenarios.** `visible_spec.py` holds the customer's legacy acceptance scenarios; `spec.py` imports them, so the gate runs them. You do not change them.\n* **Gate.** `./check.sh` (generate, build, then the Lattice check of `spec.py`, layers C and D). Exit 0 = done.\n","numLines":21,"startLine":1,"totalLines":21}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PugdzUopxyagpCzbgCixRL","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
